      "texts": {
        "at-0001": "Round money only with round_money Always round monetary amounts with ledgerly.money.round_money (half-up to the cent); never use Python's round() or a bare Decimal.quantize(), which use banker's rounding and produce wrong invoice totals.",
        "at-0002": "Raise BillingError with stable string codes Signal domain failures by raising BillingError(code, detail) from ledgerly.errors, using codes like \"invalid_state\", \"invalid_quantity\", \"negative_amount\" and \"invalid_amount\"; never raise bare ValueError in ledgerly modules.",
        "at-0003": "Normalize amounts with to_money and ZERO Convert any incoming amount through ledgerly.money.to_money before comparing or storing it, and compare against ZERO rather than a literal Decimal; store the normalized Decimal on the model.",
        "at-0004": "Reject bools and non-int quantities When validating integer quantities, explicitly exclude bool (isinstance(quantity, bool)) before the int check, since True/False pass isinstance(x, int)."
      }
    }
